Suwayomi host — provenance and licenses

The compatibility layer is built on Suwayomi-Server
(https://github.com/Suwayomi/Suwayomi-Server), licensed under the Mozilla
Public License 2.0. It is included unmodified as the git submodule
vendor/suwayomi at the commit pinned by the superproject; the host never edits
that tree. MPL-2.0 text: LICENSE-MPL-2.0.

The host under host/src/main is MoeReader's own implementation of this app's
binary wire protocol over that tree. It is not a copy of Suwayomi's server
(no Javalin, GraphQL, database, downloader or updater) and it is not a copy of
any other project's host. Files that do adapt existing work say so in their
headers:

- host/src/main/kotlin/moe/reader/suwayomi/net/NativeNetInterceptor.kt
  Adapted from the Oneechan runtime's NativeNetInterceptor
  (https://github.com/leros1337/oneechan-runtime, MPL-2.0). The file keeps its
  MPL-2.0 header.
- host/src/overlay/java/com/googlecode/dex2jar/ir/ts/NewTransformer.java
  dex2jar's file (Apache-2.0) as modified by the Oneechan runtime, then
  modified for MoeReader. The file stays Apache-2.0; both modifications are
  named in its header.
- host/src/main/kotlin/moe/reader/suwayomi/Extensions.kt
  The dex2jar builder configuration is copied from Suwayomi-Server's
  PackageTools.dex2jar (MPL-2.0); the exception handler and logging are
  MoeReader's.
- host/build.gradle.kts
  The vendor include/exclude lists started from the Oneechan runtime's
  source-api build (MPL-2.0 configuration) and were then changed for this app.

The app-side Swift (MoeReader/SuwayomiCompat) and the JNI shim implement this
project's wire format (SuwayomiWire.swift and Wire.kt). The Oneechan runtime
repository contains no app-side Swift, and no file in it was copied into
MoeReader/SuwayomiCompat.

Third-party libraries are resolved by Gradle and keep their own licenses; the
runtime the app bundles is licensed separately in jvm-ios/NOTICE.
